  "question": {
    "text": "If \\(y=\\frac{x}{\\log _e|c x|}\\) is the solution of the differential equation \\(\\frac{d y}{d x}=\\frac{y}{x}+\\phi\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)\\), then \\(\\phi\\left(\\frac{x}{y}\\right)\\) is given by"
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{y^2}{x^2}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(-\\frac{y^2}{x^2}\\)",
      "is_correct": true
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(\\frac{x^2}{y^2}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    },
    {
      "text": "\\(-\\frac{x^2}{y^2}\\)",
      "is_correct": false
    }
  ],
  "correct_answer": [
    "B"
  ],
  "solution": {
    "text": "Hint : \\(y=\\frac{x}{\\ell n|c x|}\\)\n\\(\\begin{aligned}\n& \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\frac{\\ell \\mathrm{n}|c x|-1}{(\\ell \\mathrm{n}|\\mathrm{cx}|)^2}=\\frac{1}{\\ell \\mathrm{n}|\\mathrm{cx}|}-\\frac{1}{(\\ell \\mathrm{n}|\\mathrm{cx}|)^2} \\\\\n& \\Rightarrow \\frac{\\mathrm{dy}}{\\mathrm{dx}}=\\frac{\\mathrm{y}}{\\mathrm{x}}-\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{y}}{\\mathrm{x}}\\right)^2 \\quad \\therefore \\phi\\left(\\frac{\\mathrm{x}}{\\mathrm{y}}\\right)=-\\frac{\\mathrm{y}^2}{\\mathrm{x}^2}\n\\end{aligned}\\)"
  }
}